${outputs.simulate_warehouse_operations.raw}

Apply each scan in order: RECEIVE adds stock at the destination, PICK removes it, TRANSFER moves it between locations, COUNT records a physical count next to the system figure. Build a movement ledger summary and the current stock position.

Expected output: (1) Current stock table: SKU, name, opening qty, received, picked, net transfers, system closing qty, last counted qty (if any), current location(s), stock value (USD), status (OK / LOW / OUT / NEGATIVE). (2) Reorder alerts: each SKU at or below its reorder point with suggested reorder quantity. (3) Rejected scans: any event that could not be applied, with the reason. (4) Totals: SKUs tracked, total units, total stock value, scans processed. If the scan log or setup is missing, empty or contains NO DATA, reply with exactly: NO DATA: warehouse scan log returned nothing — estimated, remembered or example values are never a substitute.

