Benchmark assumptions for the manual process (state them in your answer): manual data entry 45 seconds per scan event; manual reconciliation 3 minutes per SKU; manual investigation 20 minutes per issue; manual processes typically catch about 60% of errors, with a 2% data-entry error rate. AI-assisted assumptions: 3 seconds per scan event, 10 seconds per SKU, 4 minutes of human review per issue.

Compute: (1) detection accuracy — injected errors caught, missed, false positives, precision and recall; (2) time for manual vs AI-assisted, time saved and % reduction; (3) estimated errors a manual process would catch vs errors the AI caught; (4) value of stock protected (units in caught issues x unit cost).

Expected output: An efficiency scorecard: the stated assumptions; a detection table (injected error, caught by AI yes/no, matching anomaly ID); precision, recall, caught/missed/false-positive counts; manual vs AI-assisted hours with time saved and % reduction; manual vs AI errors caught; stock value protected (USD); and 3-5 headline metrics suitable for a demo slide. If any input is missing, empty or contains NO DATA, reply with exactly: NO DATA: demo results returned nothing — estimated, remembered or example values are never a substitute.

